### Try with multiple catch block
- Every type of exception the ways of handling is different.
- Used when multiple exceptions can occur in a single try block
- Each catch handles a specific exception
- Prevents program crash and improves readability

Syntax
try {
    // risky code
} catch (ExceptionType1 e) {
    // handle exception 1
} catch (ExceptionType2 e) {
    // handle exception 2
}

** Rules:-

- Order matters: child exception first, parent last
- Only one catch executes for an exception
- Exception class should be last catch block
